msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Background {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Periodic boundary conditions connect the last qubit in a chain to the first. If these qubits are far apart on a quantum processor, implementing their interaction requires routing, which can add two-qubit gates and increase circuit depth.\n"
msgstr "Ikinokonekta ng periodic boundary conditions ang huling qubit sa isang chain sa una. Kung magkalayo ang mga qubit na ito sa isang quantum processor, nangangailangan ng routing ang pagpapatupad ng interaksyon nila, na maaaring magdagdag ng mga two-qubit gate at magpataas ng circuit depth.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gate cutting replaces a two-qubit gate with a weighted combination of single-qubit operations and measurements. Executing these experiments and combining their results reconstructs expectation values for the original circuit. This can reduce routing overhead, at the cost of additional sampling. See the [circuit cutting explanation](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/explanation/index.html) for the underlying quasiprobability decomposition.\n"
msgstr "Pinapalitan ng gate cutting ang isang two-qubit gate ng weighted na kombinasyon ng mga single-qubit na operasyon at measurement. Ang pagpapatakbo ng mga experiment na ito at pagsasama ng mga resulta nila ay bumubuo muli ng mga expectation value para sa orihinal na circuit. Maaari nitong bawasan ang routing overhead, kapalit ng karagdagang sampling. Tingnan ang [circuit cutting explanation](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/explanation/index.html) para sa pinagbabatayang quasiprobability decomposition.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You will first validate this workflow on a six-qubit noiseless simulator. Then you will apply it to a chain of at least 30 qubits on hardware and compare the cut and uncut results. The circuit uses parameters with analytically known expectation values, so the hardware comparison does not require a large statevector simulation.\n"
msgstr "Unang i-validate ang workflow na ito sa isang six-qubit na noiseless simulator. Pagkatapos, ilalapat mo ito sa isang chain na may hindi bababa sa 30 qubit sa hardware at ihahambing ang mga resulta ng cut at uncut. Gumagamit ang circuit ng mga parameter na may analytically known na mga expectation value, kaya hindi nangangailangan ang paghahambing sa hardware ng malaking statevector simulation.\n"

