msgid "Import the tools used in both examples. Aer supports the intermediate measurements introduced by gate cutting.\n"
msgstr "I-import ang mga tool na ginagamit sa parehong halimbawa. Sinusuportahan ng Aer ang mga intermediate measurement na ipinakilala ng gate cutting.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa sa maliit na simulator {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use a six-qubit ring with two layers of entangling gates. The simulated device has linear connectivity, so the ring's closing edge requires routing unless it is cut.\n"
msgstr "Gumamit ng six-qubit na ring na may dalawang layer ng mga entangling gate. May linear connectivity ang simulated na device, kaya ang pangwakas na edge ng ring ay nangangailangan ng routing maliban kung puputulin ito.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: I-map ang mga classical input sa isang quantum na problema {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following function creates RX rotation layers interleaved with CX gates on alternating edges of the ring. Two repetitions give two boundary gates to cut. Set the first two rotation layers to zero and the final layer to $\\pi$. The ideal output is then $|1\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, up to a global phase.\n"
msgstr "Gumagawa ang sumusunod na function ng mga RX rotation layer na magkakahalinhinan sa mga CX gate sa magkakahalinhinang edge ng ring. Ang dalawang repetition ay nagbibigay ng dalawang boundary gate na puputulin. Itakda sa zero ang unang dalawang rotation layer at sa $\\pi$ ang huling layer. Ang ideal na output ay $|1\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, hanggang sa isang global phase.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure the average single-qubit Z expectation and the average adjacent ZZ expectation, **including the periodic pair**:\n"
msgstr "Sukatin ang average na single-qubit Z expectation at ang average na katabing ZZ expectation, **kasama ang periodic na pares**:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M_Z = \\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}\\langle Z_i\\rangle, \\qquad\n"
"C_{ZZ} = \\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}\\langle Z_i Z_{(i+1)\\bmod n}\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M_Z = \\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}\\langle Z_i\\rangle, \\qquad\n"
"C_{ZZ} = \\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}\\langle Z_i Z_{(i+1)\\bmod n}\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Their ideal values are $-1$ and $+1$, respectively. These parameters provide a benchmark for the workflow; they do not demonstrate a classically difficult computation.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga ideal na halaga nila ay $-1$ at $+1$, ayon sa pagkakabanggit. Nagbibigay ang mga parameter na ito ng benchmark para sa workflow; hindi nila ipinapakita ang isang computation na mahirap para sa classical.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Six-qubit periodic circuit with two boundary CX gates](/docs/images/tutorials/periodic-boundary-conditions-with-circuit-cutting/extracted-outputs/periodic-06-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Six-qubit periodic circuit with two boundary CX gates](/docs/images/tutorials/periodic-boundary-conditions-with-circuit-cutting/extracted-outputs/periodic-06-1.avif)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pagpapatupad sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create a device model with a linear coupling map. It supplies the compilation target; the execution in Step 3 will be noiseless.\n"
msgstr "Gumawa ng device model na may linear na coupling map. Nagbibigay ito ng compilation target; magiging noiseless ang execution sa Step 3.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add a **virtual connection** between the physical qubits at the ends of the chain. Transpile once using this augmented coupling map and a CX basis. The virtual connection prevents the transpiler from routing the boundary gates, but the resulting circuit cannot run on the real device yet.\n"
msgstr "Magdagdag ng **virtual connection** sa pagitan ng mga physical qubit sa magkabilang dulo ng chain. I-transpile nang isang beses gamit ang augmented coupling map na ito at isang CX basis. Pinipigilan ng virtual connection ang transpiler na i-route ang mga boundary gate, pero hindi pa mapapatakbo ang nagreresultang circuit sa totoong device.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find and cut the two boundary CX gates, apply the virtual layout to the observables, and generate all decomposition terms with `num_samples=np.inf`. This makes the decomposition coefficients exact; the measurements still use a finite number of shots.\n"
msgstr "Hanapin at i-cut ang dalawang boundary CX gate, ilapat ang virtual layout sa mga observable, at buuin ang lahat ng decomposition term gamit ang `num_samples=np.inf`. Dahil dito, eksakto ang mga decomposition coefficient; gumagamit pa rin ng may hangganang bilang ng shot ang mga measurement.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, translate the experiments into the device's native gates and correct their direction where needed. These passes preserve the physical qubit layout and avoid repeating layout selection and routing for every experiment. The helper returns the mapped observables needed for reconstruction.\n"
msgstr "Panghuli, i-translate ang mga experiment sa native gate ng device at ayusin ang direksyon ng mga ito kung kinakailangan. Pinapanatili ng mga pass na ito ang physical qubit layout at iniiwasan ang pag-uulit ng layout selection at routing para sa bawat experiment. Ibinabalik ng helper ang mga mapped observable na kailangan para sa reconstruction.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each CX decomposition has six terms. With two cuts and one shared Z measurement basis, this produces $6^2=36$ experiments. The sampling overhead is a different quantity: the squared sum of the absolute decomposition coefficients is $9^2=81$. It describes the sampling cost of maintaining precision under quasiprobability reconstruction. See the [sampling overhead explanation](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/explanation/index.html).\n"
msgstr "Anim na term ang bawat CX decomposition. Sa dalawang cut at isang shared na Z measurement basis, nagreresulta ito sa $6^2=36$ experiment. Ibang dami ang sampling overhead: ang squared sum ng mga absolute na decomposition coefficient ay $9^2=81$. Inilalarawan nito ang sampling cost ng pagpapanatili ng precision sa ilalim ng quasiprobability reconstruction. Tingnan ang [paliwanag tungkol sa sampling overhead](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/explanation/index.html).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For comparison, transpile a measured copy of the uncut circuit using the actual coupling map. `measure_all()` records the original logical qubits in the `meas` register; transpilation preserves that classical-bit mapping, so its counts can be evaluated with the original observables.\n"
msgstr "Para sa paghahambing, i-transpile ang isang measured na kopya ng uncut circuit gamit ang aktwal na coupling map. Itinatala ng `measure_all()` ang orihinal na logical qubit sa `meas` register; pinapanatili ng transpilation ang classical-bit mapping na iyon, kaya maaaring suriin ang mga count nito gamit ang orihinal na mga observable.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Isagawa gamit ang Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run both versions with the Aer Sampler V2 primitive. Each cut experiment receives 10,000 shots, as does the single uncut circuit. The cut workflow therefore uses 36 times as many shots in this comparison. Matching shots per circuit does not match the total execution budget.\n"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang parehong bersyon gamit ang Aer Sampler V2 primitive. Tumatanggap ng 10,000 shot ang bawat cut experiment, gayundin ang nag-iisang uncut circuit. Kaya 36 na beses na mas maraming shot ang ginagamit ng cut workflow sa paghahambing na ito. Ang pagkakapareho ng shot bawat circuit ay hindi nangangahulugan ng pagkakapareho ng kabuuang execution budget.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reconstruct each Pauli expectation value using the same mapped observables and experiment order used during generation. Then average the first $n$ values for $M_Z$ and the remaining $n$ values for $C_{ZZ}$. For the uncut circuit, calculate the expectation values directly from the measured counts.\n"
msgstr "I-reconstruct ang bawat Pauli expectation value gamit ang parehong mapped observable at experiment order na ginamit sa paggawa. Pagkatapos, i-average ang unang $n$ value para sa $M_Z$ at ang natitirang $n$ value para sa $C_{ZZ}$. Para sa uncut circuit, kalkulahin ang mga expectation value nang direkta mula sa mga nasukat na count.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Ideal, cut, and uncut expectation values from noiseless simulation](/docs/images/tutorials/periodic-boundary-conditions-with-circuit-cutting/extracted-outputs/periodic-16-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Ideal, cut, and uncut expectation values from noiseless simulation](/docs/images/tutorials/periodic-boundary-conditions-with-circuit-cutting/extracted-outputs/periodic-16-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The noiseless results should be close to the ideal values. Finite-shot reconstruction can fluctuate, and a reconstructed estimate can lie outside $[-1,1]$. Cutting does not improve an already noiseless result; this example verifies the decomposition, layout mapping, and reconstruction before execution on hardware.\n"
msgstr "Dapat malapit sa mga ideal na value ang mga noiseless na resulta. Maaaring magbago-bago ang finite-shot reconstruction, at maaaring lumampas sa $[-1,1]$ ang isang reconstructed na estimate. Hindi pinapabuti ng cutting ang resultang noiseless na; bine-verify ng halimbawang ito ang decomposition, layout mapping, at reconstruction bago ang execution sa hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa ng malakihang hardware {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reuse the workflow on the least-busy operational QPU with at least 120 qubits. Select a longest shortest path in its undirected coupling graph: each consecutive pair is connected, while the endpoints are far apart. This adapts the chain to the selected device instead of relying on a fixed Eagle layout. The code checks that the chain contains at least 30 qubits and that its endpoints are not neighbors.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin muli ang workflow sa pinakakaunting-pila na operational na QPU na may hindi bababa sa 120 qubit. Pumili ng isang pinakamahabang shortest path sa undirected coupling graph nito: konektado ang bawat magkasunod na pares, habang magkalayo ang mga dulo. Inaangkop nito ang chain sa napiling device sa halip na umasa sa nakapirming Eagle layout. Tinitiyak ng code na may hindi bababa sa 30 qubit ang chain at hindi magkapitbahay ang mga dulo nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following block combines the four steps. Gate twirling, measurement twirling, and dynamical decoupling are disabled for both versions. Both jobs run in the same batch and receive the tutorial tag `TUT_CCPBC`. The cut experiments still use more total shots, so compare both accuracy and QPU usage.\n"
msgstr "Pinagsasama ng sumusunod na block ang apat na hakbang. Naka-disable ang gate twirling, measurement twirling, at dynamical decoupling para sa parehong bersyon. Tumatakbo ang dalawang job sa iisang batch at tumatanggap ng tutorial tag na `TUT_CCPBC`. Mas marami pa ring kabuuang shot ang ginagamit ng mga cut experiment, kaya ihambing ang parehong accuracy at QPU usage.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Ideal, cut, and uncut expectation values measured on ibm_boston](/docs/images/tutorials/periodic-boundary-conditions-with-circuit-cutting/extracted-outputs/periodic-19-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Ideal, cut, and uncut expectation values measured on ibm_boston](/docs/images/tutorials/periodic-boundary-conditions-with-circuit-cutting/extracted-outputs/periodic-19-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the recorded run on `ibm_boston`, the cut estimates were approximately $M_Z=-0.923$ and $C_{ZZ}=0.896$, compared with $-0.611$ and $0.516$ for the uncut circuit. Both cut estimates were closer to the ideal values of $-1$ and $+1$.\n"
msgstr "Sa naitalang run sa `ibm_boston`, ang mga cut estimate ay humigit-kumulang $M_Z=-0.923$ at $C_{ZZ}=0.896$, kumpara sa $-0.611$ at $0.516$ para sa uncut circuit. Parehong mas malapit ang mga cut estimate sa mga ideal na value na $-1$ at $+1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-27
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare each result with its ideal value and inspect the circuit depths and total QPU usage. Cutting removes the need to route the periodic gates, but introduces intermediate operations and additional statistical uncertainty. Hardware noise and calibration affect the comparison; an improvement is not guaranteed. Repeated runs are needed to assess whether an observed difference is statistically significant.\n"
msgstr "Ihambing ang bawat resulta sa ideal na value nito at suriin ang mga circuit depth at kabuuang QPU usage. Inaalis ng cutting ang pangangailangang i-route ang mga periodic gate, pero nagpapakilala ito ng mga intermediate operation at karagdagang statistical uncertainty. Nakakaapekto sa paghahambing ang hardware noise at calibration; hindi garantisado ang pagbuti. Kailangan ang paulit-ulit na mga run upang masuri kung statistically significant ang naobserbahang pagkakaiba.\n"

